## 4. OSPF — Open Shortest Path First

OSPF is a link state routing protocol — routers build a
complete map of the network topology and calculate best
paths independently.

### OSPF Characteristics
- Metric: Cost — based on interface bandwidth
- No hop count limit — scales to large networks
- Fast convergence — detects changes quickly
- Sends updates only when topology changes — not periodic
- Uses areas to scale large networks
- Industry standard — widely used in enterprise networks

### OSPF Cost Calculation
Cost = Reference bandwidth / Interface bandwidth
Default reference bandwidth = 100 Mbps

| Interface | Bandwidth | Cost |
|-----------|-----------|------|
| Serial | 1.544 Mbps | 64 |
| FastEthernet | 100 Mbps | 1 |
| GigabitEthernet | 1000 Mbps | 1 |

*Note: FastEthernet and GigabitEthernet both show cost 1
with default reference bandwidth — adjust reference
bandwidth for accurate cost calculation*

### OSPF Areas
- **Area 0 (Backbone)** — all OSPF networks must connect
  to or through area 0
- **Regular areas** — connect to area 0
- Areas reduce routing table size and limit LSA flooding

### OSPF Configuration

! Basic single area OSPF
R1(config)# router ospf 1
R1(config-router)# router-id 1.1.1.1
R1(config-router)# network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
R1(config-router)# network 10.0.0.0 0.255.255.255 area 0
R1(config-router)# passive-interface GigabitEthernet0/1
R1(config-router)# auto-cost reference-bandwidth 1000
R1(config-router)# exit
! Verify OSPF
R1# show ip ospf
R1# show ip ospf neighbor
R1# show ip ospf database
R1# show ip route ospf
R1# show ip ospf interface GigabitEthernet0/0

### OSPF Authentication

! MD5 authentication per interface
R1(config)# interface GigabitEthernet0/0
R1(config-if)# ip ospf authentication message-digest
R1(config-if)# ip ospf message-digest-key 1 md5 0spfP@ssw0rd
R1(config-if)# exit

### OSPF vs RIP Comparison

| Feature | RIP | OSPF |
|---------|-----|------|
| Type | Distance vector | Link state |
| Metric | Hop count | Cost (bandwidth) |
| Max hops | 15 | Unlimited |
| Convergence | Slow | Fast |
| Updates | Every 30 seconds | On change only |
| Scalability | Small networks | Large networks |
| CPU/Memory | Low | Higher |
| Standard | Open | Open |

