## 6. Routing Security Best Practices

### General Routing Security
- Use authentication on all routing protocols
- Use passive-interface on interfaces that should not
  send routing updates
- Apply ACLs to filter routing updates
- Monitor routing table for unexpected changes
- Use static routes where topology is simple and stable

### Passive Interface
Prevents routing updates being sent out an interface
while still advertising the connected network:

! Stop RIP updates going to end user network
R1(config)# router rip
R1(config-router)# passive-interface GigabitEthernet0/0
R1(config-router)# exit
! Stop OSPF hello packets on interface
R1(config)# router ospf 1
R1(config-router)# passive-interface GigabitEthernet0/0

### Route Filtering

! Create prefix list to filter routes
R1(config)# ip prefix-list FILTER_IN seq 5 deny 10.0.0.0/8
R1(config)# ip prefix-list FILTER_IN seq 10 permit 0.0.0.0/0 le 32
! Apply to routing protocol
R1(config)# router ospf 1
R1(config-router)# distribute-list prefix FILTER_IN in

