## 8. Troubleshooting Routing

### Systematic Approach Using OSI Model

! Step 1 — Check physical connectivity
R1# show interfaces GigabitEthernet0/0
! Step 2 — Check IP addressing
R1# show ip interface brief
! Step 3 — Check routing table
R1# show ip route
! Step 4 — Test connectivity
R1# ping 192.168.2.1
R1# traceroute 192.168.2.1
! Step 5 — Check routing protocol
R1# show ip protocols
R1# show ip ospf neighbor

### Common Routing Problems

| Problem | Symptom | Check |
|---------|---------|-------|
| Interface down | Route missing from table | show interfaces |
| Wrong subnet mask | Partial connectivity | show ip interface |
| Missing network statement | Route not advertised | show ip protocols |
| Authentication mismatch | Neighbour not forming | show ip ospf neighbor |
| ACL blocking traffic | Ping fails with route present | show access-lists |

